# `render` before another operator: DS0120, with a fix that moves it to the end.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | render barchart | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..40
  PIPELINE@0..39
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    RENDER_OP@15..30
      IDENT@15..21 "render"
      WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
      IDENT@22..30 "barchart"
    WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
    PIPE@31..32 "|"
    WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
    TAKE_OP@33..39
      IDENT@33..37 "take"
      WHITESPACE@37..38 " "
      LITERAL@38..39
        LONG@38..39 "5"
  WHITESPACE@39..40 "\n"

error[DS0120]: `render` must be the last operator
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | render barchart | take 5
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^   ------ this operator comes after `render`
  |                |
  |                the chart is drawn at this point
  |
  = help: move `render barchart` to the end of the query

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | take 5 | render barchart
which parses without errors
